Package: fpcalib
Title: Calibration of a Bayesian False-Positive Occupancy Model under Detection Heterogeneity
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Diogo B.", "Provete", email = "dbprovete@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")))
    # TODO: add co-authors and ORCIDs before submission (do not invent identifiers)
Description: Simulation-based calibration of a Bayesian false-positive
    (misclassification) single-season occupancy model fit in Stan, with a
    head-to-head comparison against the frequentist occuFP estimator from
    unmarked. The package simulates acoustic occupancy data under homogeneous,
    unstructured (Beta), and structured ("confusion species") false-positive
    regimes, fits both models to each dataset, and scores 95% interval coverage
    and bias for the false-positive rate (p10), nightly use (psi), and the
    occupancy slope (b1). Supporting material for the JAV-03737 software note.
